e in the French army carries a Field Marshall wand in his knapsack.","When firmness is sufficient, rashness is unnecessary.","In politics... never retreat, never retract... never admit a mistake.","Courage is like love; it must have hope to nourish it.","There are only two forces that unite men -- fear and interest.","Truth alone wounds.","The human race is governed by its imagination.","True heroism consists in being superior to the ills of life, in whatever shape they may challenge us to combat.","Four hostile newspapers are more to be feared than a thousand bayonets.","In politics, an absurdity in public business is going into it.","A throne is only a bench covered with velvet.","Let the path be open to talent.","Secrets travel fast in Paris.","A people which is able to say everything becomes able to do everything.","Riches do not consist in the possession of treasures, but in the use made of them.","It requires more courage to suffer than to die.","There are two levers for moving men -- interest and fear.","The greatest general is he who makes the fewest mistakes.","Do you wish to find out the really sublime? Repeat the Lord\u0027s Prayer.","The only victory over love is flight.","Who saves his country violates no law.","He who fears being conquered is sure of defeat.","Great people are meteors designed to burn so that the earth may be lighted.","My downfall raises me to infinite heights.","Doctors will have more lives to answer for in the next world than even we generals.","The best way to keep one\u0027s word is not to give it.","A leader is a dealer in hope.","The torment of precautions often exceeds often exceeds the dangers to be avoided. It is sometimes better to abandon one\u0027s self to destiny.","Music of all the arts has the most influence on the passions and the legislator should give it the greatest encouragement.","The only King of France worthy of the name","A Constitution should be short and obscure.","From the heights of these pyramids, forty ce