457000202	61.0	["Louis Bonaparte","Jérôme Bonaparte","Joseph Bonaparte","Napoleon Louis Bonaparte"]	["I tell you Wellington is a bad general, the English are bad soldiers; we will settle this matter by lunch time.","When soldiers have been baptized in the fire of a battle-field, they have all one rank in my eyes.","A true man hates no one.","If you want a thing done well, do it yourself.","Nothing is more difficult, and therefore more precious, than to be able to decide.","Water, air, and cleanness are the chief articles in my pharmacy.","The infectiousness of crime is like that of the plague.","Medicine is a collection of uncertain prescriptions, the results of which, taken collectively, are more fatal than useful to mankind.","\\Ability is nothing without opportunity.\\","We must laugh at man to avoid crying for him.","The only one who is wiser than anyone is everyone.","Alexander, Caesar, Charlemagne, and myself founded empires; but what foundation did we rest the creations of our genius? Upon force. Jesus Christ founded an empire upon love; and at this hour millions of men would die for Him.","The extent of your consciousness is limited only by your ability to love and to embrace with your love the space around you, and all it contains","Ability is of little account without opportunity.","The people to fear are not those who disagree with you, but those who disagree with you and are too cowardly to let you know.","Do you know what amazes me more than anything else? The impotence of force to organize anything.","Chance is the providence of adventurers.","Glory is fleeting, but obscurity is forever.","\\Never interrupt your enemy when he is making a mistake.\\","The future destiny of the child is always the work of the mother.","Great ambition is the passion of a great character. Those endowed with it may perform very good or very bad acts. All depends on the principals which direct them.","I made all my generals out of mud.","Victory belongs to the most persevering.","Public opinion is the thermometer a monarch should constantly consult.","Incidents should not govern policy; but, policy incidents.","Occupation is the scythe of time.","The great proof of madness is the disproportion of one\u0027s designs to one\u0027s means.","Medicines are only fit for old people.","There are only two forces in the world, the sword and the spirit. In the long run the sword will always be conquered by the spirit.","You must not fight too often with one enemy, or you will teach him all your tricks of war.","One must change one\u0027s tactics every ten years if one wishes to maintain one\u0027s superiority.","Power is my mistress. I have worked too hard at her conquest to allow anyone to take her away from me.","The art of government is not to let me grow stale.","Men are lead by trifles.","A celebrated people lose dignity upon a closer view.","If you wish to be success in the world, promise everything, deliver nothing.","In politics, an absurdity is not a handicap.","You must not fear death, my lads; defy him, and you drive him into the enemy\u0027s ranks.","The conscience is the sacred haven of the liberty of man.","Impossible is a word only to be found in the dictionary of fools.","There is no place in a fanatic\u0027s head where reason can enter.","Public instruction should be the first object of government.","The most dangerous moment comes with victory.","The herd seek out the great, not for their sake but for their influence; and the great welcome them out of vanity or need.","Character is victory organized.","Men are Moved by two levers only: fear and self interest","With audacity one can undertake anything, but not do everything.","Respect the burden.","There is no class of people so hard to manage in a state, as those whose intentions are honest, but whose consciences are bewitched.","The best cure for the body is a quiet mind.","When I want any, good head work done; I always choose a man, if possible with a long nose.","Every privat